{
 "id": "CACHE-11-keep-warm-off-pending",
 "note": "0.1.11: the cache output says what keep-warm did in the current idle gap. A gap keep-warm refused before its first ping (one keep_warm_stop row, pings 0, refused true; an older plugin's no-idle-path row with no start row counts too) reads keep_warm.off = its reason and `· keep-warm off (<why>)` on the line, until a main request after it. A keep_warm_send row (a ping going out) reads keep_warm.pending true and `· ping pending` until its keep_warm_ping or keep_warm_stop row. A late ping is last_result late. Right after a compaction the context is nearly empty, so the line reads `cache compacted` and the new `label` key reads compacted; `state` stays cold and `why` compacted (v1 stays additive). With no main request time to bound it (caching off, no transcript), keep_warm.off lasts at most an hour after its row. A ping out for over 150 s with no result row (its process died) is no longer pending.",
 "now": "2026-11-09T12:00:00Z",
 "tz": "UTC",
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "a refused gap: one stop row, why no-jobs, refused",
